tress, etc.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, can be grumpy, can be uncooperative. Also we have weak memory for numbers, wrong tone, nasty remarks (from Agent 3). So reliability high, stress high, technical decent, but crew cooperation issues.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. So reliability high, crew cooperation positive, but communication difficulty and egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills. Also from Agent 1 notes: D is regarded as arrogant, weak leadership.\n\nWe need to decide recommendation. Let's evaluate criteria:\n\n- Operational reliability: A unknown, B very conscientious, C 100% reliable, D unknown.\n- Stress resilience: A unknown, B handles stress well, C keeps calm in crisis, D responds adequately.\n- Technical competence: A strong (anticipate dangerous, complex connections, spatial vision), B good (weather, computer), C understands complicated tech, D solves problems extremely well.\n- Decision quality: A unknown, B unknown, C can make correct decisions quickly, D solves problems extremely well (maybe decision quality).\n- Attention and information accuracy: A can be unorganized, B weak memory for numbers, C unknown, D can concentrate very well.\n- Crew cooperation: A not good at criticism, unorganized, maybe poor; B nasty remarks, uncooperative; C creates positive atmosphere, but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric; D arrogant, weak leadership.\n- Professional communication: A not good at criticism, maybe poor; B wrong tone; C difficulty communicating; D arrogant.\n- Responsibility: A unknown, B unknown, C unknown but reliable, D takes responsibility seriously.\n- Adaptability: A not good at criticism, not open to new ideas; B can be grumpy; C not willing to further education; D arrogant.\n\nThus strongest overall seems Candidate C: reliability, calm, decision quality, technical, positive crew atmosphere (though communication difficulty). Candidate B has reliability and stress but crew issues. Candidate D has responsibility and concentration but crew issues and arrogance. Candidate A has technical but many concerns.\n\nThus I would likely support Candidate C as the best overall, but need to address concerns. I can argue that C's communication difficulty and egocentric attitude are mitigated by positive crew atmosphere and reliability, and that adaptability can be trained. Also note that B's crew cooperation issues are more severe (nasty remarks). So I will vote for Candidate C.\n\nI need to reference prior discussion: Agent 2 recommended C, Agent 3 recommended B. I will support Agent 2, argue that C's reliability and crew atmosphere outweigh B's interpersonal issues. Provide evidence: C is 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, keeps calm, makes correct decisions quickly. Also note that B's nasty remarks are serious.\n\nThus my public message: I agree with Agent 2, recommend Candidate C, explain why.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
